Runtime: Context

Purpose:
  Define the context engine and knowledge resolution system for
  the SDDRA runtime. Determines which .sdd entities and project
  knowledge are loaded for each task execution, optimizing for
  token efficiency, relevance, and security.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  Context resolution protocol
  Graph-based knowledge retrieval
  Semantic + graph hybrid retrieval
  Token budget management
  Context priority and staleness
  Context versioning
  Agent context isolation
  Knowledge sharing between parallel tasks

Principles:
  Minimal context is better than full context.
  Agent sees only authorized and relevant subgraph.
  Context is resolved per task, not per project.
  Stale context MUST be detected and refreshed.
  Token budget is enforced at context injection time.

ContextResolution:
  protocol:
    1. Receive task
    2. Resolve task requirements
    3. Traverse graph to required depth
    4. Filter by permissions
    5. Filter by relevance
    6. Apply token budget
    7. Prioritize by criticality
    8. Inject into agent context

  rule: context resolution is deterministic
  rule: full project dump is NEVER sent

GraphRetrieval:
  depth_query:
    definition: traverse graph N levels from task node

    example:
      TASK-500
        ↓ dependencies (depth 1)
      TASK-400, TASK-401
        ↓ skills (depth 2)
      SKILL-GO, SKILL-TEST
        ↓ policies (depth 3)
      POLICY-SEC-01

  rule: default depth is 2
  rule: depth is configurable per task type

HybridRetrieval:
  architecture:
    User Task
      |
      |-- Semantic Search -> relevant documents
      |
      |-- Graph Search -> structurally related entities
              |
              ↓
         Context Merger
              |
              ↓
            Agent

  rule: semantic search finds similar content
  rule: graph search finds required relationships
  rule: merger deduplicates and prioritizes

TokenBudget:
  definition:
    maximum tokens allocated for context

  allocation:
    system_rules: 10%
    project_rules: 15%
    domain_rules: 15%
    skill_rules: 20%
    task_context: 30%
    agent_context: 10%

  rule: budget is enforced before injection
  rule: overflow MUST be logged and reported

ContextPriority:
  levels:
    CRITICAL:
      - task requirements
      - acceptance criteria
      - required skills

    HIGH:
      - dependencies
      - policies
      - architecture constraints

    MEDIUM:
      - domain context
      - related APIs
      - related entities

    LOW:
      - historical context
      - similar tasks
      - documentation

  rule: CRITICAL context is NEVER trimmed
  rule: LOW context is first to be trimmed on budget overflow

StaleContext:
  detection:
    - entity updated after context was loaded
    - dependency changed
    - policy changed

  handling:
    - invalidate cache
    - re-resolve context
    - re-inject fresh context

  rule: stale context MUST NOT be used for execution decisions

ContextVersioning:
  rule: context snapshots are versioned with execution
  rule: context version is recorded in execution record
  rule: context replay MUST be possible for debugging

ContextSharing:
  parallel_tasks:
    rule: shared context is read-only
    rule: each task gets its own mutable context copy
    rule: synchronization points share only required deltas

KnowledgeManager:
  responsibilities:
    - read .sdd registry
    - update skill cache
    - share context between agents
    - synchronize with .sdd/
    - validate knowledge freshness

ContextIsolation:
  rule: agent MUST NOT see unauthorized entities
  rule: security-sensitive entities are filtered
  rule: context is scoped to task boundary

ContextOptimization:
  techniques:
    - cache frequently used contexts
    - lazy load skills
    - compress intermediate results
    - reuse token budgets
    - predictive skill loading

Navigation:
  Runtime: @INDEX.sdd
  Agent: @agent.sdd
  Session: @session.sdd
  Orchestrator: @../orchestrator/INDEX.sdd
  Skills: @../skills/INDEX.sdd
  Graph: @../graph/INDEX.sdd
  Protocol: @../protocol/INDEX.sdd

Rules:
  [RT-CTX-01] Context MUST be minimal and relevant — never full project dump.
  [RT-CTX-02] Context resolution is deterministic — same task gets same context.
  [RT-CTX-03] Token budget is enforced before context injection.
  [RT-CTX-04] Stale context MUST be detected and refreshed.
  [RT-CTX-05] Agent context isolation reduces token cost and attack surface.
  [RT-CTX-06] Graph traversal depth is configurable per task type.
  [RT-CTX-07] Hybrid retrieval combines semantic and graph search.
  [RT-CTX-08] Parallel tasks share read-only context; mutable copies are isolated.
  [RT-CTX-09] CRITICAL context is never trimmed; LOW context is first trimmed.
  [RT-CTX-10] Context version is recorded with execution for reproducibility.
  [RT-CTX-11] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to context outputs.
  [RT-CTX-12] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in context output headers or titles — reserved for human use only.

State: +
